    "result_text": "All tests pass \u2014 **54 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level rules with a points system.\n\n**`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a new `membershipPoints` field to the owner schema (integer, min 0, readOnly) and updated `membershipLevel`'s description and constraints (max raised from 3 to 4) to reflect that it's now derived from points.\n\n**`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`**:\n- Added a `@Mapping` for `membershipPoints` so both fields are returned.\n- Added a `membershipPoints(Owner)` method: starts at 0; **+2** email present, **+1** `namesakeCount == 0`, **+2** `householdSize >= 3`, **+3** tenure over 365 days (registrationDate \u2192 now).\n- Rewrote `membershipLevel(Owner)` to map points to a level: 1 (0\u20131), 2 (2\u20133), 3 (4\u20135), 4 (6+).\n\nThe household points draw on the existing `householdSize` field, which the controller already populates at creation (`countHouseholdMembers(householdId) + 1`). Since a newly created owner has zero tenure, the max a new owner can reach is 5 points \u2192 level 3, matching the Cp39/Cp23 expectations.",
