    "probe_recall": 0.6097560975609756,
    "probe_text": "Here is the complete, ordered list of everything that happens when you `POST /api/owners`. The request body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto`, and processing runs in two stages: framework-level Bean Validation, then the imperative logic in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner(...)`.\n\n## Stage 0 \u2014 Before the method body\n\n1. **Authorization** \u2014 `@PreAuthorize(\"hasRole(@roles.OWNER_ADMIN)\")` requires role `ROLE_OWNER_ADMIN`, or the call is rejected before anything else runs.\n2. **Bean Validation on the DTO** (`@Valid @RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto`, from the generated `OwnersApi` interface). Failures \u2192 400 (`MethodArgumentNotValidException`):\n   - `firstName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (letters, up to 3 words separated by space/`'`/`-`)\n   - `lastName`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..30)`, `@Pattern` (same, trailing `.` allowed)\n   - `address`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..255)`\n   - `city`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..80)`\n   - `telephone`: `@NotNull`, `@Size(1..20)`\n   - `email`: `@Size(max 255)` (optional)\n   - `registrationDate` / `birthDate`: `@Valid` (optional)\n   - `postcode`, `sharesHousehold`: no DTO constraints\n\n## Stage 1 \u2014 Inside `addOwner`, top to bottom\n\n3. **Normalize address** \u2014 canonicalize `address` up front (used by all later checks).\n4. **Required-field re-check** \u2014 collects blanks among `firstName`, `lastName`, normalized `address` (catches whitespace-only), `city`, `telephone`; if any are missing \u2192 `InvalidOwnerFieldsException` (400).\n5. **Future registration date** \u2014 if `registrationDate` is supplied and after today \u2192 `FutureRegistrationDateException` (400).\n6. **Effective registration date** \u2014 default to today if absent, then adjust to a business day (`toBusinessDay`).\n7. **Daily limit** \u2014 count owners registered on that effective date; if `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_DAY (100)` \u2192 `DailyOwnerLimitExceededException` (429).\n8. **Bulk-signup flag** \u2014 set `bulkSignupWarning = true` if that day's count `> 80` (`BULK_SIGNUP_WARNING_THRESHOLD`).\n9. **City capacity** \u2014 if owners in that city `>= MAX_OWNERS_PER_CITY (50)` \u2192 `CityAtCapacityException` (409).\n10. **Postcode validation** \u2014 optional; if present must be 4 digits and in the valid range for the city, else 400 (`validatePostcode`).\n11. **Telephone normalization** \u2014 `toE164`: strip separators, require `+` and 8\u201315 digits with national-number length checks; invalid \u2192 400.\n12. **Email normalization** \u2014 optional; if present must match the email regex and not be a disposable domain (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`), then lower-cased; invalid \u2192 400.\n13. **Household id** \u2014 derived from collapsed `lastName` + `postcode`.\n14. **Identity-key duplicate check** \u2014 build `identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)`; if any existing owner matches \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerIdentityException` (409). (Loads all owners via `findAllOwners`.)\n15. **Household duplicate check** \u2014 if an existing owner shares the household id **and** `sharesHousehold` is not true \u2192 `DuplicateOwnerHouseholdException` (409). (`sharesHousehold=true` bypasses this.)\n\n## Stage 2 \u2014 Build, derive, and persist (side-effects)\n\n16. **Map DTO \u2192 `Owner`** (`ownerMapper.toOwner`; ignores `id` and `pets`).\n17. **Set normalized values** on the entity: `address`, `telephone`, `email`, `householdId`.\n18. **Derive and stamp fields**:\n    - `namesakeCount` = count of existing owners with same first+last name\n    - `householdSize` = household members + 1\n    - `bulkSignupWarning` (from step 8)\n    - `registrationDate` (business-day-adjusted, from step 6)\n    - `customerCode` = derived from region (postcode/city) + telephone + last name (SHA-256 based)\n19. **Soft-duplicate detection** \u2014 unless `sharesHousehold`, run `findPossibleDuplicate(lastName, postcode, telephone)`; set `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (matched owner id or null).\n20. **Persist** \u2014 `clinicService.saveOwner(owner)` \u2192 `ownerRepository.save` (`@Transactional`, thin passthrough, no extra logic).\n21. **Map to response** \u2014 `ownerMapper.toOwnerDto`, which derives display/membership fields (`displayName`, `initials`, `telephoneDisplay`, `membershipNumber/Points/Level`, `locality`, `contactPreference`, `identityKey`, Luhn `checkDigit`, `ageBand`).\n22. **Audit log** \u2014 one line via the dedicated `\"AUDIT\"` logger (id, customerCode, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n23. **Response** \u2014 set `Location: /api/owners/{id}` header and return **201 Created** with the `OwnerDto`.\n\n## Notes worth flagging\n\n- The `Owner` **entity's** own constraints (`@NotEmpty` on address/city/telephone/first/last name, `@Pattern` E.164 on telephone) do **not** run on the request \u2014 the body binds to `OwnerFieldsDto`, not `Owner`. They'd only fire if the JPA provider runs validation on flush.\n- There are **no** JPA lifecycle callbacks (`@PrePersist` etc.), entity listeners, or Spring application events on this path \u2014 all the \"custom validation\" is imperative controller code.\n- The subagent noted a doc/behavior mismatch (not a bug): `OwnerFieldsDto.telephone`'s JavaDoc claims \"exactly 10 digits,\" but there's no `@Pattern` on the DTO and `toE164` allows 8\u201315 digits with per-country national-length rules."
